# Daily encrypted hindsight bank dump → your fork.
#
# Replace REPO_PATH with the absolute path to your hermes-agent-workflow
# clone, then `crontab -e` and paste the line below (uncommented).
#
# What this does: at 03:44 local time, runs per-table `pg_dump` on the
# hindsight Postgres database. Small tables go to
# hindsight-data/<table>.sql; bulk tables (memory_units, memory_links)
# are byte-rotated into hindsight-data/<table>/NNNN.sql chunks ≤ 80 MB
# each (so the dump fits under GitHub's 100 MB per-blob cap). git-crypt
# encrypts via the `hindsight-data/**` rule, commits + pushes.
# Restore on a fresh host via scripts/restore-hindsight-bank.sh.
#
# OFF BY DEFAULT. Same prerequisites as sync-hermes-state — see that
# .cron.example file.

# 44 3 * * * REPO_PATH/scripts/sync-hindsight-bank.sh >> ~/.hermes/logs/sync-hindsight-bank.log 2>&1
